{-
   Snapshots on JavaScript, which there is no store for - Design-Test.md §11.2's F4 note.

   `lib/File.yana` is written in terms of Native's platform file and a JS build has no descriptors,
   so there is no filesystem on this target and nothing here pretends there is one. What `snapshot`
   does instead is **skip, loudly**: the call is counted, a `skip` line goes on the report stream and
   the case neither passes nor fails on it. That is ruling 4 applied to the target rather than to the
   file - an assertion that did not happen must say so - and it is the same answer `@test(aborts)`
   gets here.

   Making this work is a `HostMember` per `fs` call plus the declarations, which is the mechanism
   `Native/Host.js.yana` already has; it is not written because nothing has asked for it yet, and a
   half-implemented one would be the lie that file's note is written against.
-}

pub fn snapshotStoreAvailable() -> Bool = False

pub fn readSnapshotFile(root: String, file: String) -> Maybe(String) = Nothing

pub fn writeSnapshotFile(root: String, file: String, text: String) -> Maybe(String) =
    Just("this target has no filesystem")

pub fn removeSnapshotFile(root: String, file: String) -> Maybe(String) =
    Just("this target has no filesystem")

pub fn snapshotFileNames(root: String) -> [String] = []
